l checks passed\\\")\n'@\n& \\\"C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe\\\" -c \"'$editScript\nif ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }\ngit diff --check\ngit diff -- docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml docs/test/test-cases.toml'","aggregated_output":"guarded edit: TOML parsed; exactly five requested cells changed; LF and no-LLR-shall checks passed\r\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\nindex 85238579c..628f15cc6 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\n@@ -3744,11 +3744,11 @@ phase = 6\n \n [design.LLR-360]\n sr_refs = [\"SR-161\", \"SR-186\"]\n-title = \"Perspective questions in a decomposition-round sitting\"\n+title = \"Perspective questions and the stopping-boundary line in a decomposition-round sitting\"\n module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/plan_briefs.py;project-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/prompts/adjudicate-first-approval.template.md;project-trajectory/prompts/adjudicate-amendment.template.md;project-trajectory/scripts/hats.py;project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py\"\n code_symbol = \"sitting_hat_block/round_hat_block/round_questions/fill_hat_slot/sitting_tail/hat_surface_for_work_item/NOT_A_ROUND/HAT_SLOT/HAT_PARENTS/_roster_refusal/compose/combined_values/context_from_work_item/_authoring_tags\"\n-detail = \"A sitting brief for a decomposition round carries every declared perspective question applicable to that round and asks the verdict to name one outcome for each perspective. The verdict's per-perspective outcome lines are neither row-ruling lines nor machine lines, so a verdict carrying them parses to the same rulings and judged rows as one without them. A decomposition round judges a system requirement awaiting first approval or an approved stakeholder need whose text is amended; another judged set carries no perspective question. The applicable set combines each amended need with each need named by a system requirement the sitting judges, including an amended system requirement, widens each need by the authoring work item's declared tags, and evaluates each need alone. A first-approval or amendment row a route mints records the declared tags of the work items that route names as its authors, and those tags stand in place of the row's own classification; a route naming no authoring work item records none, and the row widens by its own tags. Such a row minted from a minted row passes that record on, so the minted and in-lane sittings for one system requirement reach one perspective set wherever the authoring work item is named. Questions fill the perspective slot only when the sitting template declares it; a template without that slot composes unchanged. A sitting composed from several judgement kinds carries the questions once. Outside a decomposition round the roster is not read. An absent roster yields its no-perspective line, while an unreadable existing roster refuses a round's composition only when its template declares the perspective slot, and names the roster.\"\n-rationale = \"A decomposition review needs the applicable questions in the same brief and verdict that record its judgement. Treating each parent need independently prevents tags from one sibling widening another, while an optional slot preserves briefs that do not conduct a decomposition review.\"\n+detail = \"A sitting brief for a decomposition round carries every declared perspective question applicable to that round and asks the verdict to name one outcome for each perspective. The verdict's per-perspective outcome lines are neither row-ruling lines nor machine lines, so a verdict carrying them parses to the same rulings and judged rows as one without them. A decomposition round's sitting brief also carries a named stopping-boundary line, asking the verdict to state, for each retained chain, why further splitting would only paraphrase or duplicate; a round with no roster or no applicable perspective carries it beside its no-perspective line, because the stopping decision rests on no perspective. A stopping-boundary line is likewise neither a row-ruling line nor a machine line, and nothing checks for it: a retained chain with no stopping reason is a finding for the review of the verdict. A decomposition round judges a system requirement awaiting first approval or an approved stakeholder need whose text is amended; another judged set carries no perspective question and no stopping-boundary line. The applicable set combines each amended need with each need named by a system requirement the sitting judges, including an amended system requirement, widens each need by the authoring work item's declared tags, and evaluates each need alone. A first-approval or amendment row a route mints records the declared tags of the work items that route names as its authors, and those tags stand in place of the row's own classification; a route naming no authoring work item records none, and the row widens by its own tags. Such a row minted from a minted row passes that record on, so the minted and in-lane sittings for one system requirement reach one perspective set wherever the authoring work item is named. Questions and the stopping-boundary line fill the perspective slot only when the sitting template declares it; a template without that slot composes unchanged. A sitting composed from several judgement kinds carries the questions and the stopping-boundary line once, after its last section, and says under which section the verdict writes those lines. Outside a decomposition round the roster is not read. An absent roster yields its no-perspective line, while an unreadable existing roster refuses a round's composition only when its template declares the perspective slot, and names the roster.\"\n+rationale = \"A decomposition review needs the applicable questions in the same brief and verdict that record its judgement. T